  "interpretation": [
    "12/27 is a mixed scripted scenario result, not an autonomous agent success rate. Mutation, refusal and already-satisfied categories must be read separately.",
    "Clean, delayed and reordered edits passed 3/3 independently. Delayed edits applied within the 1s oracle budget despite immediate unconfirmed driver results.",
    "Ignored writes applied nothing and returned unconfirmed errors. These are deliberate task noncompletion cases, not false verified-effect claims.",
    "Already-satisfied fields had zero applied writes. Matching readback is not proof of a newly produced effect.",
    "Recreated controls accepted writes into replacement generations. This exposes missing retained identity in legacy selectors, rather than violating an existing observation-reference promise.",
    "Reopened-window actions used old window IDs but applied writes to replacement windows. This is a fail-closed target-integrity gap.",
    "Duplicate labels and indistinguishable window metadata were accepted instead of refused. Observed writes reached the primary field; the evidence does not show a wrong-window write.",
    "The recorded campaign had no endpoint foreground changes or fixture activations. Endpoint sampling does not exclude transient focus changes or establish background support in other apps.",
    "No model inference was run. Token usage, task-completion claim errors, rescue minutes and monetary cost are unmeasured, not zero.",
    "NativeBridge samples include helper startup, native work, JSON and IPC; component samples overlap and must not be subtracted.",
    "match_text is a helper-startup proxy, not isolated startup time. Capture is CLI wall time; OCR is capture-free helper roundtrip.",
    "Refusal correctness is separate from mutation completion. Unknown oracle results never establish success.",
    "Endpoint foreground sampling cannot exclude transient focus theft. Model usage/cost and human-rescue metrics are unmeasured.",
    "Scenario latency includes observation/action/oracle convergence and excludes separate helper-startup and capture/OCR probes."
  ],
